# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# This repo is edited on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but its working tree is
# served to Linux guests as the /vagrant synced folder, where scripts are
# executed directly. A CRLF-converted script fails on the guest with
# `$'\r': command not found` or `bad interpreter` — so without this, a fresh
# clone or checkout on Windows silently breaks every bootstrap script.
*.sh text eol=lf
